timestamp=2026-10-29T22:49:03.580Z level=INFO run=39d388d6 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/evidence/notes.txt <<'EOF'\nFinding: VULN-20261029-001\nAsset: https://uisp.ui.com/adopt\nTested at: 2026-10-29T22:48Z (UTC)\nTest identity: Account A (qacct1a6967) authenticated UISP session\nBundle: https://uisp.ui.com/home/static/js/main.ca315773.js\nSHA-256: a88cae365fd9a42f0a39605da3e1649004d57151e1a158f2c6cdcfdc1a3c4dd1\n\nObservation 1 (confirmed open redirect, http/https/ftp only):\n- Loaded:\n  https://uisp.ui.com/adopt?deviceUrl=http%3A%2F%2F127.0.0.1%3A8765%2F&deviceName=TESTDEVICE123&token=abc123\n- The page rendered \"Add device 127.0.0.1 to your UISP?\" with a Cancel button.\n- Clicking Cancel changed the top-level URL to http://127.0.0.1:8765/,\n  which returned the marker page UISP_REDIRECT_REACHED.\n- Evidence screenshots:\n  01-adopt-page-with-attacker-deviceUrl.png\n  02-cancel-redirected-to-local-server.png\n\nObservation 2 (javascript: rejected, so this is NOT XSS):\n- Loaded deviceUrl=javascript:document.title='UISPXSS'\n  Result: app rejected input and redirected to https://uisp.ui.com/setup;\n  document.title remained \"UISP Portal\". No script execution.\n- Loaded deviceUrl=%09javascript:document.title='TABXSS' (leading tab)\n  Result: same rejection; no script execution.\n- Static analysis: validator.js isURL() default protocols are\n  http, https, ftp (require_valid_protocol=true); javascript: is rejected\n  before the sink executes.\n\nSink (minified bundle):\n  Cancel button onClick:\n    onClick:function(){const e=new URL(s);window.location.href=e.href}\n  where s = URLSearchParams.get(\"deviceUrl\").\n\nRelated code-level concern (UNRESOLVED, not confirmed):\n- The same component executes tee(s,a,d) when connectionString `a` is present:\n    function tee(e,t,r){const n=new URL(e);\n      n.searchParams.append(\"controllerUrl\",t);\n      n.searchParams.append(\"token\",r);window.location.href=n.href}\n- \"Add to UISP\" triggers:\n    GET https://unms-go.ubnt.com/api/installations/unifi-controllers/<id>/connection-string\n  and stores the response as connectionString. The subsequent render calls\n  tee(), sending that controller connection string to the attacker-controlled\n  deviceUrl as the controllerUrl query parameter.\n- Could not verify end-to-end because Account A has no UISP controllers\n  (list-controllers returns {\"controllers\":[]}) and creating a paid/cloud\n  controller trial was intentionally not performed.\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
